    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: a19370ee225232700a3b5213ef2443b730dc4310 -->\n**Verdict: Needs changes before merge.** One label-logic gap in the skill; the rest checks out. Docs only, so nothing to build.\n\n**What looks good**\n- The four edits agree: same label name, yellow colour, and rule (no blockers -> `needs-maintainer`; blockers -> `needs-rework`). The PR-reviewer verdict line and AGENTS.md sentence match.\n- Table rows have the right column count: 3 cells in the SKILL.md table and in the README table, matching their headers.\n- The `needs-maintainer` label exists on GitHub (yellow, #FBCA04), and #359 and #364 carry it.\n- No closing keywords (`Fixes`/`Closes`/`Resolves`) in the body or diff. The diff touches only the four files named in the body.\n\n**Must fix (blocking)**\n1. `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md`, step 2b rule bullets. Only the \"Not built\" bullet sets `needs-maintainer`. None of the other bullets removes it. So a yellow PR that later gets a clean review keeps `needs-maintainer` next to `merge-ready`, and a yellow PR that gets blockers keeps it next to `needs-rework`. That breaks the \"every reviewed PR carries exactly the labels its state calls for\" rule stated just above the table. Fix: in the clean `MERGEABLE` bullet, the clean `CONFLICTING` bullet and the blocking bullet, also remove `needs-maintainer`, e.g. \"remove `needs-rework`, `conflicts` and `needs-maintainer`\". Only the \"Not built\" bullet keeps it.\n\n**Optional (not blocking)**\n- The SKILL.md paragraph quotes the user as \"that needs-maintainer needs to / into the skill right?\". That is a dictation fragment. Tidy it to the intended wording.\n\nLabel set: `needs-rework` (this PR is already a draft, so no draft change is needed). It is not flagged ready. Push the fix as a plain push, then re-review.\n",
